course: dictionary
lesson: 14345
title: Offender: a person who has done wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An offender is a person who has broken the law or done a crime. The word comes from «offend», which means to do wrong or upset someone. When you meet offender in a text, look for clues like police, court, judge or broke the law.
explain: «The judge said the offender must pay a fine.» A judge decides what happens to someone who has broken the law, so offender must mean the person who did the crime. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The person who did the crime must pay a fine» still makes sense.
explain: Offender can also mean a person or thing that causes a problem. «The worst offender for leaving dishes in the sink was my brother.» Nobody is in trouble with the police here. It means he does this more than anyone else, so he is the biggest offender.
fact: An offender is a person who has broken the law or done a crime.
fact: The word offender comes from offend, which means to do wrong or upset someone.
fact: «Young offender» means a young person who has broken the law.
fact: «First-time offender» means someone who has broken the law for the first time.
fact: «Repeat offender» means someone who keeps doing the same wrong thing or breaking the law again.
fact: In everyday talk, the «worst offender» is the person who does a certain wrong most often, such as being late or leaving dishes out.
exercise: «The judge said the offender must pay a fine.» What is an offender in this sentence? | A fine paid to the court | A person who is a judge | A lawyer who helps people | *A person who has broken the law
exercise: «The worst offender for leaving dishes in the sink was my brother.» What does worst offender mean? | A dish that is dirty | *The person who does this most often | The person who washes up | The best helper in the kitchen
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the person who broke the law in «The police caught the offender by the river.» | caught | river | *offender | police
test: «Mia said Ben was a repeat offender for being late, because he was late every single day.» What does repeat offender suggest? | *Someone who keeps doing the same wrong thing | Someone who likes to repeat stories | Someone who is new to school | Someone who is always on time
test: Oliver says offender means a sweet treat. What does offender really mean? | A small animal that lives in the woods | A person who sells sweets | A person who has won a prize | *A person who has done wrong or broken the law
exam: «The offender was caught stealing bikes.» What is the best meaning of offender here? | A police officer who fixes bikes | *A person who broke the law by stealing | A person who owns a bike shop | A bike that is very fast
